        }
      ],
      "mergeID": null,
      "parentID": "677c333df9b0ab46a9f5ce76",
      "pinned": false,
      "postDeleted": false,
      "postID": "677bebb007f767c51816e9bf",
      "private": false,
      "reactions": null,
      "restoredAt": null,
      "sourceFeatureExtractionItemID": null,
      "sourceLink": null,
      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "@{60e326bd050eff14d32b9976|full_name} Yes and no, the problem is for a \"meaningful\" rating, they would need to load and measure avatars on the fly. A \"good\" avatar can easily be worse than a very poor if you mess up the animator completely, which is not covered by the performance rank at all. The current ranking system gives you \"hints or rather a general direction\" towards what you can expect, but not what might truly be. (And before you ask, yes there are very poors outperforming good rated avatars - definetely not the standard though)\n\nYou would incentivize avatar creators to care more once the \"with 70.001 polys you are very poor - period - regardless if everything else is good or better\" is adjusted to reflect some sort of \"steps\" like the other ranking factors. \n\nBut anyways, thumbs up for the default \"hide very poor\", IF i can turn that setting back to \"show all\" without having to manually show everyone, just like Swingly suggested.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    }
  ],
  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2025-01-06T14:41:52.041Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "deletedBy": null,
  "details": "On Android, the default minimum performance rank is Medium, but on PC it is VeryPoor.\n\nI feel like there's a mismatch here, PC could at least incentivize Poor or better by blocking VeryPoor by default.\n\nTo clarify, this is not hiding VeryPoor all the time unless manually shown, it is just the default block setting.\n\n(picture shows proposal, current default is Don't Block)",
